  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_00c34ec0ece94e93ae8dc8d988a28e85",
      "statement": "POST /api/tasks returns the response with a pending task row before any long-running work begins; the worker pipeline runs inside an `after()` callback from `next/server` so the serverless function is not frozen after the response is flushed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L220-L243",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2bf6b51365c0062a705296fd2d9ffbee26e5082f428aaba20a69969efe55e3ab:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L48-L250",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b2fb4b782672ab88d391ebfc135434322ca038a1b81b42c8faebf94c9de4873:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52b2f76efd1a423993aec61a438c5005",
      "statement": "The `tasks` Postgres row is the contract between the synchronous API and the asynchronous worker: the worker mutates `status`, `progress`, `logs`, `sandboxId`, `sandboxUrl`, `branchName`, `agentSessionId`, `mcpServerIds`, and `completedAt` as the lifecycle progresses, and every UI surface polls the row for live state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L394-L518",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5040cb0660ee887acc04ef66a5e70e00060450b389b0684924e34c46dba51d83:"
